    "# \ud83c\udfd7\ufe0f ConvNeXt-Tiny Siamese \u2014 Building Damage Assessment (EBD)\n",
    "### Dedicated Training & Evaluation Pipeline for Kaggle Cloud GPUs\n",
    "**Honors Project (Session 2026-2027)** | *Shri Ramdeobaba College of Engineering and Management, Nagpur*\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "### \ud83d\udd0d Why Previous Runs Showed Unrealistic Scores (`0.9987` F1 / `1.0000` Loc_F1):\n",
    "1. **The Mask Fallback Bug (Root Cause)**: If mask filenames did not match the pattern `pre_disaster_target`, the dataset silently fell back to reading the pre-disaster RGB image as the mask! The model was literally asked to segment high-brightness pixels of the input image (`loc_mask = image > 127`), which a 28M parameter ConvNeXt trivially fits to 1.0000 F1.\n",
    "2. **Overlapping Tile Leakage**: Random 80/20 splitting placed overlapping 512x512 tiles of the exact same satellite pass in both train and validation.\n",
    "3. **Zero Augmentation**: The model memorized fixed pixel grids instead of learning damage invariants.\n",
    "\n",
    "### \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f What Is Fixed in This Notebook:\n",
    "- **Strict Mask Verification**: Never uses the satellite image as a mask; validates ground truth labels.\n",
    "- **Disaster-Event-Aware Split**: Train and Validation use images from **completely different natural disaster events** (zero data leakage).\n",
    "- **Full Albumentations Pipeline**: Flips, 90\u00b0 rotations, scale-shift-rotate, color jitter, cutout, and noise.\n",
    "- **Realistic Benchmark Target**: Overall Score ~`0.70 - 0.76` (matching official xView2 / EBD state of the art).\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "### \u26a1 How to Train Offline (Shut Down Laptop & Let Kaggle Train):\n",
    "1. Under **Notebook options** (right sidebar) \u2192 **Accelerator**: Select **GPU P100** or **GPU T4 x2**.\n",
    "2. Under **Notebook options** \u2192 **Internet**: Toggle to **ON**.\n",
    "3. Click **+ Add Input** \u2192 select your **EBD dataset**.\n",
    "4. Click the blue **Save Version** (top right) \u2192 Choose **Save & Run All (Commit)** \u2192 Click **Save**.\n",
    "5. **You can now close your browser, turn off Wi-Fi, and go offline!** Kaggle runs the training in the cloud and saves `ConvNeXt_Siamese_best.pth` in the **Output** tab."
   ]
  },
